title: Public Instruction and Fine Arts
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: psoe_in_government and public_instruction_minister_party = "PSOE"
on-arrival: education_science_timer += 9; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/labarraca.jpg
go-to: ed_menu
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Education and Science

The Second Republic considers education one of its main duties as a way to transform a nation with a high illiteracy into a modern, secular and democratic country. Education received a significant boost towards the end of Alfonso XIII's reign, yet Spain remains far behind other European nations.

Current educational curriculum - [+ major_curriculum +], [+ minor_curriculum +]

Teachers' Staff - [+ education_teachers +]/3.

Schools Built - [+ schools_built +]/3.

[? if education_mix_classrooms == 1: Coeducation (mixed-gender classrooms) is legally enforced. ?] [? if education_mix_classrooms == 0: Coeducation (mixed-gender classrooms) isn't legally enforced. ?]

@ed_menu
view-if: not last_advisor_action

- @hire_teachers
- @build_schools
- @mixed_classrooms
- @structure
- @curriculum
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@hire_teachers
title: Train and hire a new cohort of Republican teachers.
subtitle: -1 Budget.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requieres at least 1 budget.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; education_teachers += 1; workers_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.1; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.2;
max-visits: 3

We drastically reform teacher training, pay higher salaries and adopt modern pedagogical standards to attract thousands of young enthusiastic men and women to the Teacher's Corp.

These new teachers become true ambassadors of the Republic across towns and villages, promoting civic values and critical thinking.

@build_schools
title: Expand urban and rural school construction.
subtitle: -1 Budget 
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Requieres at least 1 budget.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; schools_built += 1; rural_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); smallholders_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); workers_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); pro_republic += 4*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.2;
max-visits: 3

We launch a massive drive to build thousands of primary schools and hundreds of secundary schools all around the country but focusing in neglected agrarian regions. For many landless peasants, this is their first contact with literacy, art and the Republic as a whole.

@mixed_classrooms
title: Implement compulsory coeducation (mixed-gender classrooms).
subtitle: Break traditional gender segregation in primary and secondary schools.
view-if: education_mix_classrooms == 0
on-arrival: education_mix_classrooms = 1; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); catholics_psoe -= 6; catholics_ap += 10; workers_ap += 4;

We declare coeducation mandatory across all state-funded primary and secondary schools. Boys and girls will learn side-by-side under the exact same curriculum, dismantling the old system that relegated girls to domestic chores and religious catechism.

While many families praise this landmark reform for equality, conservative associations and catholics denounce it as an "immoral attack on natural modesty."

@structure
title: Change the structure and funding of education.

Education in Germany has traditionally been organized on religious and class lines. Schools are often either Protestant or Catholic (or rarely Jewish), and religious classes are required in most mixed-denomination schools. In addition, the working class has at most eight years of public education in primary and middle schools, while the middle and upper classes have access to private schools and Gymnasiums that prepare students for universities. Thus, the universities tend to be dominated by conservatives and reactionaries, which has negative consequences for bureaucratic recruitment.

- @secularize
- @public_hs
- @school_boards
- @ed_menu: Do not change school funding or organization.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@secularize
title: Secularize education and replace religious order schools.
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Requieres at least 1 budget and having avoided cesions to the Catholic Chuch.
choose-if: budget >= 1 and modus_vivendi == 0
view-if: secularized = 0 and constitution_drafted_seen = 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; secularized = 1; pro_republic += 6*(1-dissent); catholics_psoe -= 15; dlr_relation -= 10; ar_relation += 6*(1-dissent); prrs_relation += 6*(1-dissent); pce_relation += 6*(1-dissent); middle_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); workers_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.5; middle_ar += 4; middle_prrs += 4; polarization += 5;

We enforce the constitutional mandate banning religious orders from teaching in secondary and primary education, nationalizing or replacing church-run schools with public statal institutions. We earn praises from other fellow republicans; however, bishops denounce indoctrination and Catholic families organize school boycotts, pushing many devout citizens into open opposition to the regime.


@curriculum
title: Reform the educational curriculum.
choose-if: curriculum_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: It is too early to change the curriculum again.

Before the Republic, classrooms were used to promote religious orthodoxy, dynastic loyalty and avoid critical thinking. Having the Public Instruction Ministery we can change the new Republican Curriculum.

What should be the major focus of our new curriculum?

- @dem_major
- @science_major
- @human_major
- @vocational_major
- @ed_menu: Do not change the curriculum now.
- @cancel_advisor_action

# note: education_science is a variable that affects how much education affects economic growth.

@dem_major
title: Democratic curriculum
subtitle: Critical thinking, democratic citizenship, and collaboration
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "democratic"; pro_republic += 5*(1-dissent); workers_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent);  middle_ar += 3; democratization += 1; dlr_relation -= 3; education_science += 0.3; polarization += 5;
go-to: curriculum_minor

We overhaul textbooks to emphasize critical thinking, scientific history, hygiene and constitutional law. Students learn about their rights as free citizens rather than subjects of a monarch or the Church. Conservative parties criticize the new texts as "politicized Republican indoctrination."

@science_major
title: Scientific curriculum
subtitle: Modern science, mathematics, and technical skills
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "scientific"; education_science += 1; prrs_relation += 4*(1-dissent); pce_relation += 3*(1-dissent); middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); workers_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); economic_growth += 0.1;
go-to: curriculum_minor

We align Spanish education with modern European standards, prioritizing physics, chemistry, natural sciences and laboratory experimentation over classical Latin and scholasticism. This helps lay the groundwork for long-term industrial modernization.

@human_major
title: Humanist curriculum
subtitle: Arts, literature, history, and philosophy
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "humanist"; middle_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.2; polarization -= 3;
go-to: curriculum_minor

Our educational curriculum should be focused on the humanities, including arts, literature, history and philosophy. Some criticize this curriculum as focusing too much on "useless" subjects, while others worry that the arts establishment is too closely tied to nationalism.

@vocational_major
title: Vocational curriculum
subtitle: Useful technical skills for future careers
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "vocational"; prr_relation += 3*(1-dissent); pce_relation += 3*(1-dissent); workers_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); rural_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); middle_psoe -= 1; unemployed -= 0.1; education_science += 0.5; economic_growth +0.3;
go-to: curriculum_minor

We establish technical and trade schools across urban centers and agricultural districts, equipping working-class youth with practical mechanical, agricultural, and industrial skills to immediately improve productivity and employment.

@curriculum_minor

And what should be a secondary focus of the curriculum?

- @dem_minor
- @science_minor
- @human_minor
- @vocational_minor

